    "updated_at": "2022-11-16T19:27:28Z",
    "body": "If so there was (probably?) an existing bug before #6315.\r\n\r\nThe previous revision (0a97a81da77bc4cb0ab5b16420605ca001ff5b17^) used _sandboxFlags_ (rather than _finalSandboxFlags_), which was plumbed in as an input to **process a navigate fetch**.\r\n\r\nI admit that state didn't make a ton of sense to me and _finalSandboxFlags_ seems to be more natural. The difference would be in the case where the response explicitly did something like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nContent-Security-Policy: sandbox\r\nCross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin\r\n```\r\n\r\nAre you confident that it should be _finalSandboxFlags_, or should we try to find someone who knows CSP/COOP to confirm?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
